apps/minecraft-plugin
# The Docker definitions themselves. Nothing COPYs them, and the Dockerfile named by `-f` is read
# from the host filesystem rather than out of the context, so excluding this directory cannot hide
# the file currently being built.
#
# This file stays at the repository root, which is the build context for every image except the
# Minecraft plugin — Docker reads .dockerignore from the context root, never from beside the
# Dockerfile, so moving it into infra/docker/ would silently stop it applying. See
# infra/docker/README.md.
infra
